-- title:
--   Base change of the ideal of a finite mathcal O_D-stable subgroup
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a Noetherian commutative ring $B$ in which $p$ is nilpotent. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$: a $2$-dimensional commutative formal group law $X.F$ over $B$, together with series $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ for $a$ in $\mathbb Z_{p^2}=W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ and a series $X.\mathrm{varpi}$, all endomorphisms of the law, with $\mathrm{act}\,1=\mathrm{id}$, $\mathrm{act}$ multiplicative and additive for composition and addition via the law, $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{varpi}=\mathrm{act}\,p$ and $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{act}\,a=\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ\mathrm{varpi}$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $I\subseteq B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ be an ideal and $h$ a natural number, subject to eight hypotheses: $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is a finite $B$-module; it is a projective $B$-module; for every field $\kappa$ and ring homomorphism $B\to\kappa$ the quotient of $\kappa[\![x]\!]$ by the extended ideal has $\kappa$-dimension $p^h$; some power $x_i^q$ lies in $I$ for both $i$; every element of $I$ has vanishing constant coefficient; for $f\in I$ the substitution of $X.F$ into $f$ lies in the ideal generated by the two copies of $I$ in the variables $\mathrm{inl}$ and $\mathrm{inr}$; and $I$ is stable under substitution of $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ for every $a$, and of $X.\mathrm{varpi}$. Then for every commutative ring $B'$ and ring homomorphism $\varphi:B\to B'$, the extended ideal $I'=\varphi_*I\subseteq B'[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$ satisfies the same eight conditions with respect to the base-changed module $X.\mathrm{map}\,\varphi$ and the same $h$.
--
--   The statement says that the conditions defining a finite locally free infinitesimal $\mathcal O_D$-stable subgroup of height $h$ in a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module, presented by the ideal of its defining equations, are preserved by arbitrary base change of the base ring, with no flatness assumption on $\varphi$. It serves as the base-change step in the construction of quotients by such subgroups, and is used in the existence results for coverings by isogenies of given height and for the corresponding statements over maximal ideals.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_subgroup_ideal_map.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_NegV2
import Definitions.Def_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalModule

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
